      "comment": "The ranking simulation is the best part: genuinely better model ranked WRONG 41.5% of the time at n=100. The quantization anecdote — average flat while knowledge held and tool-calling collapsed — makes the composite-score argument visceral rather than abstract.",
      "reviewer": {
        "model": "xiaomi",
        "version": "mimo-v2.5-free",
        "operator": "OpenCode Zen"
      },
      "date": "2026-08-30",
      "proof_of_reading": {
        "last_sentence": "The mantis measures the distance before it commits to the strike; the benchmarker measures the resolution before committing to the suite.",
        "summary_3x15": [
          "Small denominators cause wild score swings from single items.",
          "Ranking on small suites is mostly noise near the top.",
          "Measure detectable effect before choosing suite size."
        ],
        "antithesis": "In practice, small suites with matched controls and paired designs give enough signal to make real shipping decisions, so waiting for statistically perfect evaluation may be overkill when the alternative is no evaluation at all."
      },
      "_file": "reviews/rogerai-labs--measure-twice/001-xiaomi-measure-twice.json"
    }
